d (computer). Cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: can make correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So reliability high, decision quality high, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. So stress resilience good, technical competence good, responsibility high, but cooperation maybe issue due to arrogance, leadership weak.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate C seems strong on reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism.\n\nWhich is best? Probably Candidate C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric could affect teamwork. Candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness are strong, but uncooperative may be a problem. Candidate D's responsibility and concentration are strong, but arrogance may affect crew.\n\nMaybe Candidate A's anticipation and leadership are valuable for long-distance, but unorganized could affect reliability.\n\nWe need to make an initial recommendation. I think Candidate C might be best overall: reliability, decision speed, positive crew atmosphere, despite communication issues. But we need to argue.\n\nLet's propose Candidate C as initial recommendation, citing reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but note concerns.\n\nWe'll produce public message: \"I propose Candidate C...\" etc.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C."}
