 D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but hot temper is concerning. Candidate A's anticipation and leadership are valuable for long-distance, but show-off and not open to new ideas are concerning for adaptability.\n\nWe might argue that Candidate A's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections is critical for safety, and leadership qualities are valuable. The concerns (show-off, not open to new ideas) could be mitigated with training, and his technical competence (spatial vision) is strong. Meanwhile, Candidate B's communication issues (nasty remarks) could be more severe. Candidate C's egocentric and communication difficulty also severe. Candidate D's hot temper could be dangerous under stress.\n\nThus we might recommend Candidate A as best overall, given strong operational reliability (anticipates danger), technical competence, leadership, and we can address his show-off attitude.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Sarah advocated C, Emily advocated B. We'll argue that A's strengths outweigh concerns and that both B and C have more serious communication issues.\n\nProvide explicit facts: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities; also regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. B handles stress well, very conscientious, but makes nasty remarks. C difficulty communicating, egocentric. D hot temper.\n\nWe need to state recommendation: Candidate A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
